description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, make exactly ONE edit: replace the following FOUR consecutive lines with the block of lines given below. The first two lines and the closing brace are unchanged; the change inserts a bounded 'most recent actual rejection' section and appends it to the returned string.

REPLACE these four consecutive lines, verbatim:
        if (found.length > 0) {
          console.warn(`[compose-lessons] source=concept-db n=${found.length} class=${failureClasses[0] ?? "none"}`);
          return `\n\nKNOWN FAILURE MODES from this substrate's own rejected composes — plans repeating these are rolled back:\n${found.map((r) => `- ${r}`).join("\n")}`;
        }

WITH these lines, verbatim:
        if (found.length > 0) {
          console.warn(`[compose-lessons] source=concept-db n=${found.length} class=${failureClasses[0] ?? "none"}`);
          // MOST RECENT ACTUAL REJECTION, one line per class, bounded (2026-09-11).
          // concept-db dedups on exact content, and appendComposeLesson mirrors
          // `class: <static guidance>` while DISCARDING the judge's reason — so that
          // corpus holds ~27 generic rules and cannot grow past the guidance map.
          // Measured: 2955 specific reasons recorded in the JSONL, median 184 chars,
          // none of which ever reached the drafter. Attach the latest reason per class
          // here. One line per class means this block is bounded by the number of
          // classes, not by the size of the corpus. Fails open to the generic rules.
          let observed = "";
          try {
            const { readFileSync: rfs } = await import("node:fs");
            const latest = new Map<string, string>();
            for (const line of rfs(COMPOSE_LESSONS_PATH, "utf8").split("\n").slice(-400)) {
              if (!line.trim()) continue;
              try {
                const rec = JSON.parse(line) as { class?: string; reason?: string };
                if (rec.class && rec.reason) latest.set(rec.class, rec.reason);
              } catch { /* skip unparseable line */ }
            }
            const rows = [...latest.entries()].slice(-8).map(([c, r]) => `- ${c}: ${r.slice(0, 300)}`);
            if (rows.length > 0) observed = `\n\nMOST RECENT ACTUAL REJECTION per class — verbatim judge verdicts on real composes, not general advice:\n${rows.join("\n")}`;
          } catch { /* observed stays empty; the generic rules below still apply */ }
          return `\n\nKNOWN FAILURE MODES from this substrate's own rejected composes — plans repeating these are rolled back:\n${found.map((r) => `- ${r}`).join("\n")}${observed}`;
        }

ANCHORING: the line containing `[compose-lessons] source=concept-db n=` occurs EXACTLY ONCE in this file, as does `if (found.length > 0) {`. Note the header string 'KNOWN FAILURE MODES from this substrate's own rejected composes' appears TWICE in the file — once here in the concept-db path and once in the JSONL fallback below. You must edit the FIRST one, the one immediately after the source=concept-db console.warn. Do NOT touch the fallback.

WHY. composeLessonsBlock builds the block of prior-failure guidance injected into the drafter's prompt. It recalls from concept-db, and concept-db deduplicates concepts on an exact match of shape + source_type + content + org_id. The mirror that populates that corpus (appendComposeLesson, same file) writes `compose failure class ${cls}: ${COMPOSE_LESSON_GUIDANCE[cls]}` and NEVER writes the `reason` argument it receives. So the corpus deduplicates down to one row per (class, static guidance) pair and cannot grow past the size of that guidance map.

MEASURED 2026-09-11. The concept-db compose_lesson corpus holds 31 rows and 27 distinct texts, every one a generic rule. /workspace/proposals/compose-lessons.jsonl holds 2955 recorded lesson events, each carrying the judge's specific verdict on a real compose, median reason length 184 characters, 695 of them class semantic_reject. The drafter is shown the 27 generalities and none of the 2955 specifics. The load-bearing fact - why a change of this kind was actually rejected - is recorded and never reaches the point of use.

WHY THIS SHAPE OF FIX. Writing reasons into the mirrored content would defeat the content dedup and grow the corpus from 31 rows to thousands, changing what a `limit: 8` retrieval means. This change instead leaves the corpus and the mirror completely alone and augments the PROMPT locally: at most one line per failure class, each truncated to 300 characters, taken from the last 400 recorded events. The block is bounded by the number of failure classes - roughly a dozen - not by the size of the corpus, so it cannot grow without bound as failures accumulate.

SAFETY. The whole addition is wrapped in try/catch and `observed` stays an empty string on any error, so an unreadable or malformed lessons file leaves the returned block byte-identical to today's. The generic rules are still emitted first and unchanged. The JSONL fallback path further down is untouched. COMPOSE_LESSONS_PATH is already a module-level constant in this file and readFileSync is already imported this same way in the fallback. No signature, no type, and no other call site changes.

